quiet.md: look fallback fonts up by name, as GPUI 0.2 did

Upstream builds each FontFallbacks entry as a family-name + weight/slant
descriptor. For "PingFang SC" that resolves to the family in PingFang.ttc
(49533 glyphs) instead of the system UI copy CoreText falls back to
(PingFangUI.ttc, 47098 glyphs) that the editor's CJK text has always been
drawn with; the outlines differ slightly, so Chinese text drew about 2%
lighter. Create the descriptor from the name (CTFontDescriptorCreateWithName
AndSize) as before. Upstream's system cascade list after the user fallbacks
stays.

